verses.text:
“For it is written in the book of Psalms,
‘Let his homestead become desolate,
and let there be no one to dwell in it,’{h}
and,
‘Let another take his office.’{i}

‘And it shall be in the last days, says God,
that I will pour out some of my Spirit on all flesh;
and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy,
and your young men shall see visions,
and your old men shall dream dreams;

And I will give wonders in the heaven above
and signs on the earth beneath,
blood and fire and a vapor of smoke;

For David says concerning him,
‘I saw the Lord always before me,
for he is at my right hand so that I may not be shaken;

He is
‘the stone that was treated with contempt by you, the builders,
which has become the head of the corner.’{d}

who through the Holy Spirit, by the mouth of our father David your servant, said:{g}
‘Why did the nations rage,
and the peoples plot vain things?

The kings of the earth took their stand,
and the rulers were gathered together,
against the Lord and against his Anointed.’{h}

No, you took up the tent of Moloch
and the star of your god Rompha,{n}
the images you made to worship;
and I will remove you beyond Babylon.’{o}
